# command-local-test — Quick local QA (Pickleball Advanced Open Play)

> **Invoke:** Type `command-local-test`, `@command-local-test`, or "run local test" for mirrored Open Play pages.

---

## Action

1. From the **Website** folder (`package.json` root), run:
   ```powershell
   npm run local-test
   ```
   This runs `Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/scripts/local-test.js` (copies the active tree from `Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/{staging|live}/` into **both** `local-page/` at repo root and `Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/local-page/`, writes hub `index.html` in each) then starts **live-server** on port **3456** and opens `/local-page/index.html`.

2. **Copy only** (no browser):
   ```powershell
   npm run local-test:sync
   ```

---

## What gets mirrored

Configured in `Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/scripts/local-test.js` (`FILES` array). Includes RSVP, check-in, and shared `js/` under the active tree.

---

## Output

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `local-page/index.html` | Hub (short URL — same content as below) |
| `local-page/...` | Mirror — **not** for deploy |
| `Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/local-page/...` | Canonical mirror — **not** for deploy |

Both mirror folders are gitignored — regenerate with `npm run local-test:sync` anytime.

---

## URL (after `npm run local-test`)

Both mirrors are identical. Short path (default browser open):

`http://127.0.0.1:3456/local-page/index.html`

Canonical path:

`http://127.0.0.1:3456/Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/local-page/index.html`

---

## Staging vs live (Open Play)

Default dev edits go to **`Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/staging/`**. **`npm run local-test`** mirrors whichever tree **`openplay-mode.json`** selects (`activeTree`: `staging` or `live`). Firebase Hosting always deploys **`advanced-open-play/live/`** — guarded by **`openplay-deploy.js`**. See **`openplay-mode.mdc`** and **`Programs/Pickleball/README.md`**.
